---

## Step 5 — Fix failures

After the report is generated:
1. For each failed test: read the failure, identify root cause in SDK code
2. Fix the SDK code (not the test, unless the test is wrong)
3. Re-run only the failing spec: npx playwright test e2e/XX-*.spec.ts
4. Iterate until it passes
5. Re-run full suite: npm run test:e2e
6. Confirm all previously passing tests still pass

Do NOT change test assertions to make tests pass. Fix the implementation.

---

## Constraints

- Do not add new features. Validation only.
- Do not mock the cursor animation — measure real DOM positions.
- Do not mock the semantic graph — query the real shadow DOM.
- AI-dependent tests (guide mode, screenshot vision):
  if no API keys in environment, use test.skip() with clear message.
  Do not fake AI responses — that defeats the evaluation.
- All tests must be deterministic. No arbitrary sleeps over 500ms
  except where explicitly specified (recovery timeout test: 16s).
- e2e/EVAL_REPORT.md must be committed alongside the test results.

---

